{{Short description|Local administrative subdivisions of Guajicutea}}

{{Administrative divisions of Guajicutea}}

The '''municipalities of the Republic of Guajicutea''' are the island state's 59 local administrative units. They sit below the 17 districts and are used for municipal government, land registry, census reporting, and local service delivery. For the broader hierarchy of local government, see [[Administrative divisions of the Republic of Guajicutea]]. In the current layer, only three urban clusters are tagged as cities: [[Waribá]], [[Tabakurí]], and [[Barikú]]. Larger urban places such as [[Waku Bá]] and [[Yukubá]] remain municipalities rather than city-tagged clusters.

District boundaries remain the main units for Assembly apportionment, but the table below lists all 59 municipalities with their district, area, population, density, and ciudad tag.

